hey guys Pete here just finished  watching the mr. robot two-hour series  finale and have to say that I really  liked how the story wrapped up I'm  feeling a lot of different things and  feeling compelled to write 3,000 words  about this right at the moment is not  one of them so this is gonna be a quick  recap reaction kind of thing where I  talk about how I interpreted the ending  season 4 episodes 12 and 13 for a story  that has kept us guessing the whole time  I feel like what happened was pretty  clear but there was a lot going on and  it's all sandwiched in between some  really emotional moments so I will recap  slash explain the ending as I see it  talk about the moments that stood out  for me and how the series played out in  relation to my expectations and  expectations is where I'll start because  coming into this I really didn't know  what to expect anymore  I really didn't like the idea of a  simulation which I talked about in my  last recap video I never really got into  the ideas that white roses machine might  be real and there were some kind of  sci-fi explanations coming but part of  what I loved about the show was the fact  that all of that stuff was somewhat  believable like anything could happen  those things that sound that outrageous  sound that equally possible in the end  we find out that everything was related  to what's going on inside Elliott's head  the final twist was that Elliott we've  been watching he was the other one he  was the mastermind which we'll get into  later and that we never actually met the  real Elliott so episode 11 closed with  White Rose committing suicide and  activating her machine we learn in  episode 12 that the alternate world we  visited wasn't actually the result of  that it was an illusion it was a world  that was made up to keep the host  Elliott busy and safe I'm mostly gonna  gloss over the first half of this  although it was definitely a great  episode of television the opening with  mr. Roboto playing was fantastic seeing  how all the irregularities in episode 11  were from this Elliott coming into the  illusion the recursive loop as mr. robot  describes him grappling with the idea  that he could take over this life that  he could be with Angela he could be  happy all of that worked really well  there were some genuinely funny moments  in episode 12 but the real answer  started to come in  second half of the finale through an  alternate form of krysta we learned  about the personalities and how his di D  works she says in order for you to fully  hear the truth first we need to discuss  Elliott's dissociative identity disorder  we hear again that the first personality  was created the day Elliot jumped out  the window  that was the protector personality the  one that Elliot created to replace his  father to protect him from intolerable  situations later he created a mother  personality she was the persecutor she  blamed Elliot for the abuse that  happened to him and insisted that he  needed to pay for it after that came a  younger version of Elliot she describes  this as someone he merged to handle the  abuse he couldn't tolerate and she says  basically that he created his own family  of sorts Elliot looks at the camera and  says I guess she doesn't know about you  bringing us to the forefront his friend  Christa then does the same she looks  right into the camera  and says that she knows us as well the  boyars who think they aren't a part of  this despite being here for all of it  goes on to explain that the other  identities thought they knew all about  its personalities but this other one  came up not too long ago and that's the  one we know in the series the hooded  Elliot that we've followed she says I  know why you did it your heart was in  the right place he wanted to shelter him  which is why you changed his past but it  was his future you really wanted to  protect that's why he went through such  great lanes to take out all the evil  that surrounded him in the real world so  you formed eff society you loved him so  much he wanted to save the entire world  so you could make it better for him no  matter the cost that's why you hit him  here turning his harsh reality into a  fantasy trapping him in an endless loop  to keep him safe until you were ready  and this is where we get the idea of  what's been going on the show goes out  of its way  explains it three different times  through mr. robot Angela and Krista  Krista it only comes in after the other  two have already explained that just to  make sure that we understand there's  several flashbacks that show us the  clues that were there so just to recap  there are five different alters the  protector which is mr. robot Elliot's  mom who is the persecutor  younger self us or the voyeurs and the  mastermind which is the Elliott that  we've been following throughout series  the mastermind was a reaction to all of  Elliott's rage and he also became the  personality that wanted to shelter  Elliott he changed things in the past so  that his father was his friend and not  this monster that was his abuser and  after he did that he went on to try to  change the world at this point of the  story he succeeded F Society they stole  the money and redistributed it whiterose  is gone the project is destroyed the  mastermind at this point has been  successful so the only thing that's left  for him to do is to let go and that  proves to be difficult we see the  mastermind wake up in a hospital room  Darlene is there waiting she reassures  him that everything we saw over the last  four seasons was in fact true F Society  v nine robbing the dais group  it all happened white rose is dead and  the mastermind explains to her that he's  only a part of Elliott which she already  knows this is where I got that  overwhelming feeling of enjoyment that  I've gotten from mr. robot so many times  that this story was telling me something  that I wanted to hear in the boardroom  we see the alters together and the  monologue was good but as the mastermind  accepts that his work is done and heads  down the hall to join the others in the  movie theater it hit me that SML had  taken me to a place I didn't know I  needed to go at the end of the day it  was a story about healing and overcoming  the things that life puts in our way  watching the mastermind come to terms  with the fact that he's only a part of  Elliot but he's done his part to make  the world a better place there's  optimism in that that I enjoy because at  times it's been a little bit hard to  imagine that there could be an ending  that would be satisfying in that way  I loved the closing sequence in the  movie theater and I loved that it was  Darlene there waiting for him when the  host Elliot wakes up Darlene said that  she bailed because she couldn't  understand what Elliot was going through  and that felt very true to life for me  of course she came up short in their  relationship she's human but she's there  for him at the end and she gets to  deliver the hello Elliot as we say  goodbye to our friend so to be clear my  understanding of the end is this we've  never met the ho  Eliot or the real Eliot we have followed  the mastermind which was the most recent  alder that came into existence to  shelter Eliot from the trauma he  experienced he created an alternate  place for Eliot that had everything he  needed to be happy except for Darlene in  the real world he set out to take down  Ecore and ultimately white rose and  everything that we saw happened in the  four seasons of mr. robot White Rose had  created the Deus group to consolidate  power and wealth and had a delusional  plan to change the world with the  machine that she built at the Washington  Township plan she killed herself after  turning the machine on because the  mastermind put her back against the wall  by stealing her money and exposing the  data screw he was able to stop the  machine by playing the game but not  before the plant was 